#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:7
msgid ""
"There are times when you want to send a message, but you don’t want it "
"sent immediately. For example, it may be after working hours for the "
"recipient. Scheduled messages can include a :doc:`priority </end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/message-priority>`, :ref:`request acknowledgements "
"<end-user-guide/collaborate/message-priority:request acknowledgements>`, "
"include :doc:`file attachments </end-user-guide/collaborate/share-files-"
"in-messages>`, and include anything that a non-scheduled message can "
"contain, except :doc:`slash commands </integrations-guide/run-slash-"
"commands>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:11
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.3, you can schedule messages to send in the future. "
"Compose a message, then select the right side of **Send** to schedule "
"when the message will be sent. You can choose from a fixed time or set a "
"custom time, and Mattermost displays both your local time and the "
"recipient’s local time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:13
msgid ""
"Compose a message and select the right side of the **Send** button to "
"schedule when the message will be sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:19
msgid ""
"From Mattermost mobile v2.28, you can schedule messages to send in the "
"future. Compose a message, then long press on **Send** to schedule when "
"the message will be sent. You can choose from a fixed time or set a "
"custom time, and Mattermost displays both your local time and the "
"recipient’s local time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:22
msgid "Manage scheduled messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:24
msgid ""
"Once you schedule a message to send in the future, that message is "
"available within the :ref:`Drafts view <end-user-guide/collaborate/send-"
"messages:draft messages>`, under the **Scheduled** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:26
msgid "You can manage scheduled messages with the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:28
msgid "**Delete scheduled post**: Confirm that you want to delete the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:29
msgid "**Edit scheduled post**: Make changes to the draft inline before its sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:30
msgid "**Copy text**: Copy the draft text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:31
msgid "**Reschedule message**: Change when the message should be sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:32
msgid "**Send now**: Confirm that you want to send the message immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:34
msgid ""
"Once a message is scheduled, you can delete, edit, and reschedule it, "
"copy the message text, or send it immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:40
msgid ""
"Once you schedule a message, file attachments are read-only and can't be "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/schedule-messages.rst:43
msgid "Troubleshoot scheduled messages"
msgstr ""

